    "raw": "Given:\n- Original price of a shirt: $60\n- Original price of a leather jacket: $90\n- Price reduction: 20%\n\nFirst, calculate the reduced price for each item:\n- Reduced price of a shirt: $60 - (20% of $60) = $60 - (0.20 * $60) = $60 - $12 = $48\n- Reduced price of a leather jacket: $90 - (20% of $90) = $90 - (0.20 * $90) = $90 - $18 = $72\n\nNext, calculate the total cost for 5 shirts and 10 leather jackets at the reduced prices:\n- Total cost for 5 shirts: 5 * $48 = $240\n- Total cost for 10 leather jackets: 10 * $72 = $720\n\nFinally, add the costs together to find the total amount Teagan will pay:\n- Total amount: $240 + $720 = $960\n\nFINAL: 960",
